meta {
  name: Raise Ticket Form
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_ticket_options
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("options are {value, label} objects with lowercase codes", function () {
    const t = res.body.message.ticket_types[0];
    expect(t).to.include.keys("value", "label");
    expect(t.value).to.match(/^[a-z0-9_]+$/);
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Returns the dropdown values for the Raise Ticket form.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_ticket_options`
  **Screen:** Raise Ticket form

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:**

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "ticket_types": [
        { "value": "bug", "label": "Bug" },
        { "value": "support", "label": "Support" },
        { "value": "feature_request", "label": "Feature Request" },
        { "value": "training_request", "label": "Training Request" },
        { "value": "question", "label": "Question" }
      ],
      "priorities": [
        { "value": "emergency", "label": "Emergency" },
        { "value": "urgent", "label": "Urgent" },
        { "value": "normal", "label": "Normal" },
        { "value": "low", "label": "Low" }
      ],
      "projects": [
        { "name": "PROJ-0029", "title": "Hamza ERPNext Implementation", "kind": "implementation" }
      ],
      "modules": ["Accounting", "Stock"]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Response fields:**

  | Field | Type | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `ticket_types[]` | `{value, label}` | Show `label`, send `value` as `ticket_type` to **Raise Ticket**. Values: `bug`, `support`, `feature_request`, `training_request`, `question`. |
  | `priorities[]` | `{value, label}` | Show `label`, send `value` as `priority`. Values, in this order: `emergency`, `urgent`, `normal`, `low`. |
  | `projects[]` | `{name, title, kind}` | The client's projects, most recently modified first. Cancelled and closed projects are left out. `kind`: `implementation` or `amc`. Send `name` as `project`. |
  | `modules` | string[] | Module names from those projects, sorted A–Z, no duplicates. Send one as `module`. |

  **Errors:**

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403 `no_client_linked`:** the signed-in user is not linked to any client company.
  - **403 `not_permitted`:** `customer` was sent for a company the user is not linked to.
  - **404 `not_found`:** `customer` was sent and does not exist.
}
